README-VI -- three vi clones, and how to pick oneThis disk carries three unrelated vi editors.  They are not versions of eachother and none is simply better; they trade differently.  All three aretrap-free, all three drive a vt100 with TERM set and no termcap file, andSYS/login already sets TERM and TERMCAP for you.------------------------------------------------------vi -- the real one------------------------------------------------------  /dd/CMDS/vi, 96 KB.  Version 1.0, 01/90, ported for OS-9/68k by Helmut  Hoheisel-Zimmermann and published on EFFO forum disk 13.  This is NOT a clone.  Its source in SRC/effo_vi is the Berkeley ex/vi  source itself -- ex_vmain.c, ex_vops.c, ex_re.c, ex_addr.c, the real  files -- 41 of them.  If what you want is the editor's exact behaviour,  down to the corners, this is the one that has it by construction rather  than by imitation.  41 :set options.  Alone in supporting `lisp', `redraw' and `hardtabs'.  It changes personality by flag, the way the original did:      vi -x file      becomes ex      vi -d file      becomes edit  Companions: expreserve and exrecover save and restore your work if the  editor is killed.  Documentation is DOC/vi/vi.doc, which is in German.------------------------------------------------------elvis -- the one with everything around it------------------------------------------------------  /dd/CMDS/elvis, 112 KB.  Elvis 1.7 by Steve Kirkendall, ported by Peter  Reinig.  Built on this disk from CMDS/archives/elvis1.7.lzh.  58 :set options, the most of the three, and the only one here with  colour/attribute handling (`charattr'), digraphs, and a configurable  `equalprg'.  It is a clone -- very close, not identical.  It arrives as a family rather than a program:      view       elvis opened read-only      ref        look a C function up from a tags file      fmt        format text      elvprsv    preserve a session across a crash      elvrec     recover a preserved session      REBUILT/vi.elvis, input.elvis, ctags.elvis  vi.elvis and view are the same binary under another name and need  CMDS/elvis present -- they exec it.  Best documented of the three: DOC/elvis holds the full man page set, and  SRC/elvis the whole 65-file source.------------------------------------------------------vi_nocio -- the small one------------------------------------------------------  /dd/CMDS/vi_nocio, 81 KB.  PVIC 1.0a, Portable VI Clone, public domain.  The smallest of the three and the plainest: the core vi command set and  the common options (autoindent, ignorecase, showmatch, tabstop) without  wrapmargin, shiftwidth, paragraphs or sections.  No source and no documentation on this disk -- it came as a binary.  Its  own `About PVIC' screen is what there is.------------------------------------------------------Choosing------------------------------------------------------  Want the genuine article, or ex mode                  vi  Want the most features, and man pages to read         elvis  Want the smallest, or are short of memory             vi_nocio  Editing this disk's CR-terminated text                any; all three                                                        are OS-9 native  If you have no preference, start with elvis: it is the one whose manual  is here to read when something does not behave.